# Cleanup: Dynamic Smart Optimization Button

This plan transforms the current optimization flow into a single, cohesive "Optimization Toggle" button that displays pothole counts and allows for quick switching between standard and safe routes.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Consolidated UI**: I will move the pothole count information directly onto the **Floating Action Button**. This button will act as the primary control for comparing the standard path vs. the "Smart Optimized" path.
> **Toggle Behavior**: Clicking the button while in "Standard" mode will trigger the Big Scan and switch to the "Safe" route. Clicking it again will return you to the fastest "Standard" route.

## Proposed Changes

### Logic Improvements

#### [MODIFY] [map_screen.dart](file:///c:/ssdd/flutter/lib/map_screen.dart)

- **State Management**:
    - Add `_isOptimizedView` boolean.
    - Store `_baseRoutePoints` and `_optimizedRoutePoints` to allow instant toggling without re-hitting the API every time.

- **Simplified Routing Flow**:
    - Update `_processRoutes` to store the "Standard" result first.
    - Update `_smartOptimizeRoute` to perform the scan and store the "Optimized" result separately.

### UI Enhancements

- **Dynamic Optimization Button**:
    - Replace the static "Smart Optimize" button with a dynamic one:
        - **Label (Standard Mode)**: `⚠️ Standard: [N] Potholes`
        - **Label (Optimized Mode)**: `✨ Smart Route: [M] Potholes`
    - Clicking it while in Optimized mode will toggle back to the Standard route (and vice versa).

- **UI Cleanup**:
    - I will keep the bottom route selection cards for users who want to see ALL alternatives, but the new button will provide the most direct "Pothole vs Speed" comparison.

